                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Wasn't around when it first came out but years later I found a demo of this in an old computer magazine and just like that I fell hook line and sinker for the 4x genre.\n\nThe underlying concept itself is still pretty fresh to this day I reckon, tactical macroscopic overland aspects accompanied by instanced combat events for the micromanagers among us.\n\nWhat really sets this game apart though is the musical score, Kieth Zizza's compositions have transcended time and still sound just as grand and majestic to this day, even now I can get lost in turn after turn waiting for what the other factions'll do with bated breath.\n\nMantera's community mods are still alive and kicking too so there's at least a handful that constiutes a solid core fanbase of people that are trying to keep this game up to date, in a manner of speaking, to the extent that one can, to this day.\n\nThe graphics are of course outdated but will still have their own charm depending on your perspective. \nHowever if you are looking for a modern day spiritual successor to Lords of Magic then I'd go for Age of Wonders 3 which scratches almost exactly the same itch or Spellforce: Conquest of Eo in second place.",
